orld  about how you want to play a character  and then you put the suit on and  it's just straight back to the drawing  board  number four the itsy bitsy spidey went  up the water spout down came the rain  and washed the spidey out andrew  garfield accidentally waterboarded  himself in his suit he'd stated i had to  get wet and i just kind of dove in and  did not realize that water on the mask  made it impossible to breathe so i was  kind of like suffocating i could not get  any oxygen i waterboarded myself luckily  his fight coordinator andy armstrong saw  how much garfield was struggling and  jumped in to get him out of the mask  immediately number five imagine being  stuck in an 88 pound suit immersed in an  unknown goo after over six hours in a  makeup chair  problematically an entire suit was  wasted in filming because it was buoyant  once immersed in the oil slash water  slash whatever else garsgard had to sit  in  so they had to poke holes all over the  thing to stop him from floating adding  to the weight of the costume was a  hidden cooling vest that was attached to  a portable refrigerator system this  saved him from having a stroke  number 6. turns out hollywood's most  romanticized kiss was a total nightmare  for toby during that steamy kissing  scene with kirsten you know the one  upside down in the rain director sam  raimi recalls water running into toby's  upside down nostrils and that he was  kind of drowning raymie said but it was  a kissing scene so he had to pretend  like it was a pleasant sweet moment for  him when in fact he was semi-drowning  number seven you could say david was  harboring bad feelings towards his  costume david harbor who played the  namesake character hellboy in the reboot  said the costume felt like a coffin and  said coffin gets really hot and  claustrophobic and then like i would get  freaked out getting the face of hellboy  on took about two hours the blending of  the eye where the latex ends that's all  like really hard 