ht ear itch  he admitted i didn't know when i said  yes that that was what was going to be  happening that i was going to be encased  in glue latex and a 40-pound suit that i  had to wear a cooling mechanism at all  times i couldn't move my head ever  number 13 the 90s were a wild time  remember eating batteries yeah us  neither arnold schwarzenegger played mr  freeze in the 1997 movie batman and  robin what's so notable about his  costume was that he had an led light in  his mouth which looked cool when he  spoke however problematically the  actor's saliva would seep into the  batteries and the batteries would leak  acid into his mouth talk about  disgusting and dangerous  number 14. at least buddy has a good  excuse for why he dusted his body with  toxic materials it was a simpler time  another even older movie of note was the  wizard of oz buddy ebsen was originally  slated to play tin man however the  makeup he wore for the role turned out  to be toxic aluminum dust he wound up in  the hospital and was eventually replaced  by jack haley  number 15. ninjas are supposed to be  quick and light on their feet nobody  thought this through for the live action  and one more nostalgic film the 1990s  teenage mutant ninja turtles movie had a  total of four actors feeling incredibly  claustrophobic in their suits they  weighed about 48 pounds each and once  the helmets were on you couldn't get  them off because the actors would need  to get rewired into their costumes which  would take around a half hour despite  these downright horrendous experiences  the actors deal with most of them would  probably take on the role again except  for maybe he who shall not be named what  suit would you be willing to deal with  to play the role let us know in the  comments and thanks for hanging out with  us here at the things
 

